# Vendored Opus DNN subset (LPCNet features, FARGAN vocoder, nnet core)

Source: https://github.com/xiph/opus @ 940d4e5af64351ca8ba8390df3f555484c567fbb,
the commit freedv/rade_c builds against, with rade_c's src/opus-nnet.c.diff and
opus-nnet.h.diff applied (MAX_CONV_INPUTS_ALL raised to 2048 for the RADE V2
decoder; export annotations). Model data (dnn/*_data.c) as generated by that
commit's ./autogen.sh. License: COPYING (BSD-3-Clause).

Only what the daemon links: speech -> features (lpcnet_enc, pitchdnn, freq,
burg, celt_lpc/pitch/kiss_fft), features -> speech (fargan) and the neural
network core (nnet, nnet_default, parse_lpcnet_weights) that vendor/rade_c's
encoder/decoder run on. Files are copied unmodified, in Opus's own layout.

Daemon-local additions:
- config.h    float build, no run-time CPU detection: SIMD is chosen at compile
              time by dnn/vec.h (SSE on x86-64, NEON on aarch64)
- celt_fatal.c  the assertion handler, taken from celt/arch.h, instead of
              vendoring the CELT codec (celt/celt.c) for it

To update: rebuild Opus at the new commit (autogen.sh, configure), apply
rade_c's patches, and re-copy the same files.
